 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZvsx4ogVRP/",
 "title": "Fastest way to know if your business idea will work",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "The creator explains that traditional methods like business plans and asking friends do not accurately predict if a business idea will work. Instead, he shares a 5-minute test consisting of three specific questions to validate any business idea.",
 "key_points": [
  "The creator's travel company achieved nearly 10 million in sales after using a 3-question validation method.",
  "Question 1: Can you name three real competitors charging real money for this right now? If yes, a market exists; if no, you are either too early or there is no demand.",
  "Question 2: Can you describe the exact person who pays, what they google the night before they buy, and how much they have spent trying to solve this? If no, you do not know your customer well enough yet.",
  "Question 3: Would 10 strangers hand you money for this in the next 30 days? (Not just think it is cool, but actually pay).",
  "Three green lights means you have something, one red light means work to do, and three red lights means you should kill it and move on."
 ],
 "content": "The fastest way to know if your business idea will work isn't a business plan or a focus group, and it isn't asking your friends. It's five minutes and three questions. I asked these three questions before I built my travel brand to nearly 10 million in sales. One, can you name three real competitors charging real money for this right now? And if you can, there's a market, and if you can't, you're either too early or there's no demand. Two, can you describe the exact person who pays, what they Google the night before they buy, and how much they've spent trying to solve this? And if you can't, I'm not sure you know your customer well enough to sell to them yet. Three, would 10 strangers hand you money for this in the next 30 days? Not, would they think it's cool, but would they actually pay? Three green lights and you've got something. One red light, you've got some work to do, and three red lights, kill it and move on. Comment or DM VALIDATE and I'll send you the prompt that runs all three checks on your idea in five minutes.",
